# Pull Request Template

Copy this template structure when creating a Pull Request. Remove all INSTRUCTION/FORMAT/EXAMPLE labels and replace examples with real content.

---

## PR Body Template Structure

```markdown
## Task: SPWT-X

**INSTRUCTION:** Replace SPWT-X with actual task ID. Fetch task details from Notion to populate all sections.

**FORMAT:** Task ID, Story reference, Type, Priority

**EXAMPLE:**
**Story:** SPWS-1 - Spell Data Architecture & Foundation
**Type:** Tech
**Priority:** Critical

---

## What Changed

**INSTRUCTION:** Provide a high-level summary (2-4 sentences) explaining what was implemented, fixed, or improved. Focus on WHAT changed, not HOW.

**FORMAT:** Concise paragraph followed by task-type-specific section (see below)

**EXAMPLE:** "Implemented three fundamental unmanaged components that form the foundation of every spell entity in the ECS architecture."

### [TASK-TYPE-SPECIFIC SECTION - Choose one below]

**INSTRUCTION:** Select the appropriate section based on task type (Feature/Tech/Bug). Remove the other two sections.

---

#### FOR FEATURE TASKS: Components/Systems Added

**INSTRUCTION:** List what was added with brief descriptions. Include quality criteria.

**FORMAT:**
```

- **`ComponentName`** - Brief description of purpose
- **`SystemName`** - Brief description of responsibility
- **`AssetName`** - Brief description

All [components/systems/features] are:

- Quality criterion 1
- Quality criterion 2
- Quality criterion 3

````

**EXAMPLE:**
```markdown
### Components Added

- **`Velocity`** - 3D movement vector using `float3` for Burst compatibility
- **`Lifetime`** - Spawn timestamp and duration for automatic cleanup
- **`SpellOwner`** - Entity reference to caster for ownership tracking

All components are:
- Blittable and Burst-compatible
- Include comprehensive XML documentation
- Use Unity.Mathematics types for optimal performance
- Follow project naming conventions
````

---

#### FOR TECH TASKS: Technical Improvements

**INSTRUCTION:** Show measurable before/after metrics demonstrating improvement.

**FORMAT:**

```
**Before:**
- Metric 1: [value]
- Metric 2: [value]

**After:**
- Metric 1: [improved value]
- Metric 2: [improved value]

**Impact:** [Summary with quantified improvement]

**Changes Made:**
- Change 1
- Change 2
- Change 3
```

**EXAMPLE:**

```markdown
### Technical Improvements

**Before:**

- Baking time: 500ms for 100 spells
- Entity Inspector: Components hidden when inactive
- Structural changes during gameplay

**After:**

- Baking time: 50ms for 100 spells (10x improvement)
- Entity Inspector: All components visible (disabled = grayed out)
- Zero structural changes during gameplay

**Impact:** 10x performance improvement, simplified debugging, better memory locality

**Changes Made:**

- Migrated all payload components to `IEnableableComponent`
- Replaced `AddComponent/RemoveComponent` with `SetComponentEnabled`
- Updated query filters to use `.WithEnabled<T>()`
- Added enableable component guidelines to DOTS architecture docs
```

---

#### FOR BUG TASKS: Bug Fix Details

**INSTRUCTION:** Explain issue, root cause, solution, and verification.

**FORMAT:**

```
**Issue:** [What was broken]

**Root Cause:** [Why it occurred - technical explanation]

**Solution:** [How it was fixed]

**Verification:**
- Bug no longer reproducible
- Regression test added
- No side effects
- Tested on platforms
```

**EXAMPLE:**

```markdown
### Bug Fix Details

**Issue:** Status effects not applied, causing NullReferenceException when spell hits enemy

**Root Cause:** `StatusEffectSystem` ran after `LifecycleSystem`, attempting to access destroyed spell entities

**Solution:**

- Added `[UpdateBefore(typeof(LifecycleSystem))]` to `StatusEffectSystem`
- Added defensive null check for entity existence
- Created regression test to prevent future occurrence

**Verification:**

- Bug no longer reproducible (tested 50+ times)
- Regression test added to `StatusEffectSystemTests.cs`
- No side effects detected in other systems
- Tested on Windows Standalone, Android, WebGL
- Stress tested with 200 concurrent spells
```

---

## 📁 Files Created/Modified

**INSTRUCTION:** List all files that were created or modified in this PR. Use directory tree format for multiple related files, or bullet list for scattered changes.

**FORMAT - Directory Tree:**

```
Directory/
├── File1.cs (description)
├── File2.cs (description)
└── Subdirectory/
    └── File3.cs (description)
```

**FORMAT - Bullet List:**

```
- Path/To/File1.cs (description)
- Path/To/File2.cs (description)
```

**EXAMPLE - Created:**

```markdown
## 📁 Files Created
```

Assets/Scripts/Components/Common/
├── Velocity.cs
├── Lifetime.cs
└── SpellOwner.cs

```

```

**EXAMPLE - Modified:**

```markdown
## 📁 Files Modified
```

Assets/Scripts/Components/Payloads/
├── DamagePayload.cs (added IEnableableComponent)
├── HealPayload.cs (added IEnableableComponent)
└── StatusEffectPayload.cs (added IEnableableComponent)

Assets/Scripts/Systems/
