### Example 3: Bug Task PR

```markdown
## Task: SPWT-23

**Story:** SPWS-4 - Spell Payload System
**Type:** Bug
**Priority:** High

---

## What Changed

Fixed NullReferenceException when applying status effects by correcting system execution order.

### Bug Fix Details

**Issue:** Status effects not applied, causing NullReferenceException when spell hits enemy

**Root Cause:** `StatusEffectSystem` ran after `LifecycleSystem`, attempting to access destroyed spell entities

**Solution:**

- Added `[UpdateBefore(typeof(LifecycleSystem))]` to `StatusEffectSystem`
- Added defensive null check for entity existence
- Created regression test to prevent future occurrence

**Verification:**

- Bug no longer reproducible (tested 50+ times)
- Regression test added to `StatusEffectSystemTests.cs`
- No side effects detected in other systems
- Tested on Windows Standalone, Android, WebGL
- Stress tested with 200 concurrent spells

---

## 📁 Files Modified
```

Assets/Scripts/Systems/
├── StatusEffectSystem.cs (added UpdateBefore attribute, null check)
└── StatusEffectSystemTests.cs (new regression test)

```

---

## Definition of Done

- [x] `StatusEffectSystem` runs before `LifecycleSystem`
- [x] Bug no longer reproducible following original steps
- [x] Status effects correctly applied before entity destruction
- [x] No `NullReferenceException` in Console
- [x] No orphaned components (verified with Memory Profiler)
- [x] Tested on Windows, Android, WebGL
- [x] Regression test added and passing
- [x] Stress tested with 200+ concurrent spells

---

## 🔑 Key Technical Decisions

1. **UpdateBefore attribute** → Explicit system ordering prevents race conditions
2. **Defensive null check** → Protects against unexpected early destruction
3. **Regression test** → Prevents future occurrence of this bug
4. **Memory profiling** → Verified no leaked components remain

---

## 🔗 References

- **Notion Task:** [SPWT-23](notion_url)
- **Story:** [SPWS-4 - Spell Payload System](notion_url)
- **Unity Docs:** [System Update Order](https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.entities@latest/manual/systems-update-order.html)
- **Documentation:** `.cursor/rules/concept/dots-architecture.mdc#system-execution-order`

---

## Notes

System execution order is now explicitly defined. All spell types (projectile, AoE, cone, self-cast) tested and working correctly.
```

